---
/*
 * Written against what the code actually does, not against a template. Every category
 * below traces to a column in raider-mate-service's schema, a scope in the Discord
 * OAuth request, or a call in src/lib. If a future change collects something new, this
 * page changes in the same commit.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/legal-layout.astro';
import { COMPANY_URL } from '../lib/brand';

export const prerender = false;

const UPDATED = '2026-08-20';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Raider Mate's hosted instance collects, why, who it goes to, and how long it is kept."
  updated={UPDATED}
>
  <h2>Who this is about</h2>
  <p>
    Raider Mate is run by{' '}
    <strong><a href={COMPANY_URL} rel="noreferrer">Phage Solutions, s.r.o.</a></strong>, a limited
    liability company registered in Slovakia at Lermontovova 911/3, 811 05 Bratislava. Company ID
    (IČO) 53151178, VAT ID (IČ DPH) SK2121316010, Commercial Register (ORSR) insert number 147154/B.
    Under the GDPR we are the controller of the personal data described here. Write to <a
      href="mailto:dpo@phage.sk">dpo@phage.sk</a
    > about anything on this page.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>the hosted instance only</strong>, the one you reach by signing in
    here and by inviting our bot. Raider Mate is free software under the AGPL and anyone may run
    their own copy. If your guild runs its own instance, whoever runs it is the controller of your
    data, not us, and this policy does not apply to them.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>From Discord, when you sign in</h3>
  <p>
    Signing in asks Discord for three permissions, and nothing beyond them: <code>identify</code>,{
      ' '
    }
    <code>guilds</code> and <code>guilds.members.read</code>. That gives us your Discord user id and
    username, the list of servers you are in, and your role ids in the server you are working with.
    The role ids are the whole basis of deciding whether you are a raid lead.
  </p>
  <p>
    These, together with your Discord access and refresh tokens, are held in a single encrypted
    cookie in your browser. We do not copy them into a database. Signing out deletes the cookie, and
    rotating our signing secret invalidates every cookie at once.
  </p>

  <h3>What the service stores</h3>
  <p>The parts that have to outlive a browser session are kept in our database:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your Discord user id and the id of the server it is attached to.</li>
    <li>
      The characters you register: name, realm, region, class, specialisation, item level, Mythic+
      score, which one is your main, and when each was last synced.
    </li>
    <li>Your signups: the status you set, any note you wrote, and any late request you filed.</li>
    <li>Your guild's events, its compositions and its bench.</li>
    <li>
      Your guild's settings: which channel events go to, its timezone, and which roles get mentioned
      or count as raid leads.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not ask for or store your email address, your real name, your payment details or your
    Discord password.
  </p>

  <h3>From Raider.IO</h3>
  <p>
    Character progression is public World of Warcraft data. We fetch it from Raider.IO using the
    character name, realm and region you registered, and cache the result. We never send them
    anything about you as a Discord user.
  </p>

  <h3>Automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Our servers keep short-lived technical logs of requests, including IP address, for security and
    for working out why something broke.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we are allowed to hold it</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>To run the service you asked for</dt>
    <dd>
      Article 6(1)(b), performance of a contract. Everything in the two lists above exists because a
      raid roster cannot be built without it.
    </dd>
    <dt>To keep it working and unabused</dt>
    <dd>
      Article 6(1)(f), our legitimate interest in security, rate limiting and debugging. This covers
      the technical logs.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    One cookie. It holds your session, it is encrypted with AES-GCM, it is <code>httpOnly</code> so no
    script can read it, and it is <code>SameSite=Lax</code> so another site cannot use it. It is strictly
    necessary to keep you signed in, which is why there is no cookie banner asking you to accept it.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no analytics, no advertising, no tracking pixel and no third-party script on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Discord</strong> handles sign-in and receives the messages the bot posts. Their privacy
      policy governs what they do with it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Raider.IO</strong> receives character names, realms and regions when we refresh progression
      data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Scaleway</strong> hosts the service, in Amsterdam in the Netherlands, inside the EU.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When Premium billing opens we intend to use <strong>Stripe</strong> as the payment processor, and
    this page will name them properly before a single payment is taken. Today no payments are processed
    and no payment data exists.
  </p>
  <p>We do not sell your data, and we do not share it for anyone else's advertising.</p>

  <h2>Where it lives</h2>
  <p>
    The database and the service run inside the EU. Discord and Raider.IO are based in the United
    States, so using Raider Mate means data reaches them under their own terms and safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The session cookie lasts until you sign out or it expires.</li>
    <li>
      When the bot is removed from a server, that server's events, signups, compositions and
      registered characters are <strong>deleted within 30 days</strong>. Re-inviting the bot inside
      those 30 days loses nothing.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can delete any character you registered, yourself, with{' '}
      <code>/character remove</code> in Discord. Its signups, its comp slots and its gear history go with
      it, immediately and permanently. The same control is coming to the dashboard.
    </li>
    <li>Technical logs are kept for a short period and then discarded.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    The deletion most people want does not need us at all: <code>/character remove</code> in Discord erases
    a character and everything attached to it on the spot.
  </p>
  <p>
    Beyond that, under the GDPR you can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, ask us to
    delete the rest of it, ask us to restrict or stop a particular use, and ask for it in a portable
    form. Write to <a href="mailto:dpo@phage.sk">dpo@phage.sk</a> and we will answer within one month.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you think we have handled your data badly you can complain to the Slovak data protection
    authority, the Úrad na ochranu osobných údajov Slovenskej republiky, or to the authority where
    you live.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Raider Mate is used through Discord, and Discord sets a minimum age for its own accounts, which
    is higher in some countries. If you are not old enough to hold a Discord account, you are not
    old enough to use Raider Mate.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes the date at the top changes with it. If a change means we start
    collecting something new, we will say so somewhere you will actually see it rather than quietly
    editing this page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
